+## 4. Root-cause note for the incident CLASS (admin-only lane — `.github/` is protected)
+
+The problem class: every auto-landing merge-conflict exit produces (a) a red run, (b) a
+`federation_ci_failed` dispatch, (c) a new board incident row, and (d) at least one
+solver cycle burned on a structurally blocked patch (witnessed live: a prior agent
+claimed #3195 at 10:45:55Z and released at ~11:0xZ without filing evidence — the
+treadmill cost is real). Meanwhile the PR Lifecycle Guard **already** labels the same
+conflict (`conflict:needs-manual`) — two parallel planes flag one conflict, and only one
+of them mints new board rows.
+
+Smallest root-cause-shaped remedy, entirely inside `.github/workflows/pipeline.yml`
+(admin-only per the #2512 protected-path routing):
+
+- Before invoking `mergePullRequest`, read the PR's GraphQL `mergeStateStatus`.
+- `DIRTY`/`UNSTABLE` → emit a clean skip ("conflicts — needs author rebase"), exit 0,
+  and suppress the `federation_ci_failed` dispatch for that class; the Lifecycle Guard
+  label is the single source of conflict truth.
+- Optional stronger variant: when policy allows, call the update-branch API first so a
+  stale-but-clean PR self-heals instead of failing.
+
+With that pre-check, this incident family disappears at the source instead of each
+instance being triaged forever — which is the outcome the task contract's root-cause
+instruction asks for.
