+## 6. Side finding during verification — latent collection-order collision (named for the owning plane)
+
+Tier-3 for this receipt caught a live, pre-existing suite-order bomb unrelated to the
+CI incident but of the exact class the loop keeps triaging: the full-suite pytest
+collection FAILED on `tests/test_episodic_memory_persistence.py` (landed by PR #3177)
+with `'memory' is not a package`. Chain, reproduced 2026-10-30T11:2xZ:
+
+1. `gateway/tests/test_stealth_dns_guards.py:38-39` prepends `gateway/` onto
+   `sys.path` at module import (collection) time — its own header comment already
+   documents this drift class ("order-dependent suite reds");
+2. `core/memory/` (a package) and `gateway/memory.py` (a module) share the top-level
+   name `memory`; a fresh `from memory... import` while `gateway/` sits in front of
+   `core/` resolves to the gateway MODULE and dies;
+3. no gateway source does a top-level `import memory` (verified: gateway code reaches
+   it only as `gateway.memory`), so the bomb stays dormant until any test imports the
+   core `memory.*` package under full-suite collection — currently exactly one file.
+
+Fixed in this WO's second file (`tests/test_episodic_memory_persistence.py`): pin
+`core/` at `sys.path[0]` order-immunely before the import, with the collision chain
+documented in-place. **Systemic recommendation (gateway owning plane):** rename
+`gateway/memory.py` (e.g. `memory_store.py`) and update its qualified importers —
+until then, any satellite test importing core `memory.*` must re-pin the path the
+same way. Not done here: cross-satellite rename is outside this triage's smallest-safe
+scope and Anti-Stampede applies to fixes too.
+
